      "content": "No, the legal legitimacy of Palestinian claims was never ignored; international law explicitly recognized the indigenous Arab population's rights through the 1922 British Mandate for Palestine. The 1947 UN Partition Plan itself codified this principle by proposing the division of land between \"two peoples in a single land,\" granting equal voting rights to both Jewish and Arab representatives on the UN partition committee. While British policy oscillated and eventually favored the Zionist argument for a one-state solution, the fundamental legal contradiction remained until the 1948 war escalated the conflict into definitive statehood.",
