      "content": "It is a common and well-documented argument in history that the establishment of Israel in 1948 effectively violated the 1947 UN Partition Plan and the 1922 British Mandate to the extent that the new state was declared illegal by the Arab Liberation Army. However, the legal \"legitimacy\" of the issue was never one-sided; while the UN and Arab states argued the state was illegal, the 1947 Resolution explicitly recognized the right of the Jewish people to a national home and state based on self-determination. Ultimately, the conflict wasn't just about legal standing but the intractable disagreement over how to interpret the right to existence in the same geographic territory.",
